 anisotropy_coupling  = 0
 TimeIntegratorOption = 1

-------------------------------------------

inputs_STT_macrospin

Spin-transfer torque (STT) test with an analytic solution.
A uniformly magnetized block with every field switched off except the two
STT fields, H_STT_DL (damping-like) and H_STT_TL (field-like), so each cell
is an independent macrospin.  With the polarization p along +z,
  mz(t)  = tanh( (t - t0)/tau ),  1/tau = mu0 |gamma| (a_J + alpha b_J) / (1 + alpha^2)
  phi(t) = phi(0) + mu0 |gamma| (b_J - alpha a_J) t / (1 + alpha^2)
The header of the inputs file tabulates mx, my, mz at t = 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1 ns
to compare with Diagnostics.txt.
==================== Initial Setup ====================
 demag_coupling       = 0
 M_normalization      = 1
 exchange_coupling    = 0
 DMI_coupling         = 0
 anisotropy_coupling  = 0
 STT_DL_coupling      = 1
 STT_TL_coupling      = 1
 TimeIntegratorOption = 2

-------------------------------------------

STT_inputs/inputs_STT_MTJ

STT switching of a perpendicular CoFeB(1 nm)/MgO(1 nm)/CoFeB(1 nm) magnetic
tunnel junction, a 40 nm diameter pillar.  The MgO barrier is the non-magnetic
(Ms = 0) layer between the fixed reference layer and the free layer.  A 1.5 ns
current pulse switches the free layer from antiparallel to parallel.
STT_DL_coupling and STT_TL_coupling turn the two STT terms on and off.
==================== Initial Setup ====================
 demag_coupling       = 1
 M_normalization      = 1
 exchange_coupling    = 1
 DMI_coupling         = 0
 anisotropy_coupling  = 1
 STT_DL_coupling      = 1
 STT_TL_coupling      = 1
 TimeIntegratorOption = 2

-------------------------------------------
